#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""docker-compose-lint: holds the Docker Desktop override of deploy/compose.yml to its shape, and holds the RESULT to the base's effective configuration (M-1b; bob@helix).

  python3 -I scripts/docker-compose-lint --base <compose.yml> --override <compose.docker.yml> [--print-merged]
      MERGE MODE. Merges the override over the base by the rules of docs.docker.com/reference/compose-file/merge/ (mappings merge, sequences append,
      command / entrypoint / healthcheck.test are replaced, the unique resources of a service (ports, volumes, secrets, configs) are keyed by their
      effective identity (ports: host ip, published, target, protocol; volumes: target; secrets and configs: target, which defaults to the source) and an
      entry with the same identity MERGES as a mapping, !override replaces, !reset removes) and checks the result with every rule below.
      --print-merged prints the merged model as JSON and checks nothing. Needs PyYAML.
  python3 -I scripts/docker-compose-lint --rendered <config.json> --secrets-dir <abs dir> --server-image <ref>
      RENDERED MODE. Checks the output of `docker compose config --format json` (on a Mac, the REAL one). Needs only the standard library.

BOTH modes run the SAME rules on the same normalised model of each service (sizes in bytes, durations in seconds, short and long syntax of ports, volumes and
secrets expanded, environment as a mapping): the EXPECT table below is the base's effective configuration, and a service must match it key by key; a key
the base does not set (privileged, cap_add, devices, a changed command ...) is itself a finding. A Compose that renders an extra key this table does not know
FAILS the lint: it fails closed.

HONEST LIMIT: the merge in merge mode is THIS FILE's implementation of the documented rules, not Compose's own merge, and the rendered fixtures of the tests are
the author's reading of the JSON shape, not a recording; the real Docker Desktop and the real macOS are NOT RUN until M-6.

Rules: DCL-01 the override has only the allowed shape; DCL-02 the result differs from the base only where the override may change it, and the services are
db, migrate and server; DCL-03 the secrets; DCL-04 images, no build, pull_policy never; DCL-05 migrate and server keep their hardening exactly; DCL-06 the
database keeps its pin, its init and publishes no port; DCL-07 every published port is the base's and on loopback; DCL-08 each service has exactly the base's mounts,
read-only where the base says so, and the secrets directory is mounted into nothing; DCL-09 each service gets exactly the base's secrets, mounted under their own
names; DCL-10 names; DCL-11 health checks exactly; DCL-12 no key the base does not set, and the base's command, restart, labels, dependencies and networks; DCL-13 the
environment exactly; DCL-14 memory, cpu and shared-memory limits exactly.
Exit codes: 0 clean; 1 findings (one line each, then a FAILED line); 2 usage or an unreadable file.
"""
